guide forever/miscellaneous/stalk-with-the-earthmother
title Stalk With The Earthmother
category Miscellaneous
faction Horde
race Tauren
levels 8-12
zone Thunder Bluff
keywords Stalk With The Earthmother, Boarton Shadetotem, Hoof-Holstered Blade, Valley Cosh, Venture Co Disguise, Seaforium Mining Charge, Blasting Supplies, Windfury Cone, Mortar and Pestle, Raw Brilliant Smallfish, Knife Set, Fish Chunks, Venture Co. Mine, Windfury Ridge, Thunder Bluff, weapon
reward item 277988 278002
why A one-hand blade or mace at 11 from Boarton Shadetotem's three tests in and around Thunder Bluff, for a Tauren of any class.

# Forever's Stalk With The Earthmother, three quests from Boarton Shadetotem in
# Thunder Bluff (Season of Discovery's Dual Wield chain, reworked):
# 76156 (five Seaforium Mining Charges from the Venture Co. Mine, in the
# disguise he gives you) -> 76160 (eight Windfury Cones ground with his
# Mortar and Pestle) -> 76240 (fillet a Raw Brilliant Smallfish in front of
# him with his Knife Set: a choice of the Hoof-Holstered Blade or the Valley
# Cosh). quests.json gives the three no prerequisites; the quest texts run in
# this order ("one last idea" on 76240).
# Who can take them: the server's own quest answers (players' quest caches,
# build 70450, two sources each) give all three the race mask of Tauren only
# (0x20), and so does the knowledge base; quests.json had Orc, Tauren and
# Troll (76240: every Horde race), from Classic-era data. Following Forever's
# data first, the guide is Tauren only (forever-db/corrections/quests.json on
# this branch sets the three to Tauren). Classes: every Tauren class gets all
# three. Forever's change notes drop the old class limits (76156 and 76160
# "Classes none", 76240 "no longer Dual Wield"), and Tauren players' dialog
# captures show a Warrior and a Druid on 76156, a Druid and a Hunter on 76160
# and a Druid, a Hunter and a Shaman on 76240. quests.json limited 76240 to Shamans
# (corrected on this branch).
# INGAME: are Orc and Troll characters turned away by Boarton (server race mask Tauren only; Forever's quest page: Orc, Tauren, Troll)?
# Objectives (data/forever now has them, 2026-11-09): 76156 five Seaforium
# Mining Charges (206157) from the Blasting Supplies carts (403041, spawns in
# and around the Venture Co. Mine, Mulgore); 76160 the Pine Salve (206175) the
# Mortar and Pestle makes from eight Windfury Cones (403105, Windfury Ridge and
# the hills north of Thunder Bluff); 76240 the Fish Chunks (206345) from the
# Knife Set. Players' recordings tick each where the guide sends them: the
# charges at the carts (57.7-60.2, 42.4-50.0), the salve on Windfury Ridge, and
# the Fish Chunks on the mesa 60 to 90 yards from Boarton (4 people), so the
# knife does not need him beside you. Boarton is stealthed (player notes).
# The pool: Thunder Bluff's main mesa (Forever's quest notes: "from a vendor
# or by fishing"); no vendor in the data sells the smallfish.
# A Tauren side guide, not a class guide: every Tauren class takes the chain,
# so it was nobody's class quest (as a Shaman class guide it showed Tauren
# Warriors, Hunters, Shamans and Druids the class-quest card and heads-up).
# The leveling guide tauren/01-mulgore does not take it: the route reaches
# Thunder Bluff only after the Venture Co. Mine and Windfury Ridge (level
# 11-12), and the chain needs Thunder Bluff before each of them.

step Boarton Shadetotem
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Boarton Shadetotem hides in stealth on the main mesa of Thunder Bluff, south of its pool: walk to where the arrow points until his outline shows. He hands you the Venture Co Disguise. The quest opens at level 4, but the mine holds Venture Co. Workers (level 8-9), Supervisors (9-10) and Supervisor Fizsprocket (12): go at 9 or 10.
  accept 76156                                -- Boarton Shadetotem

step The Venture Co. Mine
  zone Mulgore
  tip Ride down the lift and south-east across Mulgore to the Venture Co. Mine. Put on the disguise, then open the carts of Blasting Supplies inside the mine and on the slope outside it; stay on the upper levels where you can, the lower tunnels are packed. Five charges.
  collect 206157 x5 quest 76156.1             -- Seaforium Mining Charge, from the Blasting Supplies

step Boarton Shadetotem
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Back to Boarton in Thunder Bluff. He gives you the Mortar and Pestle for his next test.
  turnin 76156                                -- Boarton Shadetotem
  accept 76160

step Windfury Cones
  zone Mulgore
  tip Windfury Cones lie on the ground under the harpies' nest trees on Windfury Ridge, north-west of Thunder Bluff; the harpies do not drop them. The Windfury Sorceresses (level 9-10) and Matriarchs (10-11) there stand close together: pick the cones from the edges. Once you have eight, use the Mortar and Pestle to grind them.
  collect 206170 "Windfury Cone" x8 optional @31.9,32.0 -- the mortar takes all eight
  use 206176 "Mortar and Pestle" quest 76160.1 @31.9,32.0 -- grind the eight cones into the Pine Salve

step Boarton Shadetotem
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Back to Boarton. He hands you the Knife Set for the last test.
  turnin 76160                                -- Boarton Shadetotem
  accept 76240

step Raw Brilliant Smallfish
  tip Buy a Raw Brilliant Smallfish at the Auction House (Auctioneer Stampi, north of the pool), or fish one yourself: Kah Mistrunner trains Fishing and Sewa Mistrunner beside him sells the Fishing Pole and a Shiny Bauble; the pool on the main mesa gives smallfish at any skill. Then use the Knife Set on it, wherever you are.
  collect 6291 x1 optional @40.4,51.8          -- Raw Brilliant Smallfish: the Auction House, or the pool; the knife takes it
  use 206344 "Knife Set" quest 76240.1 @41.7,59.9 -- fillet the smallfish into Fish Chunks (where players did it, on the way back to Boarton)

step Boarton Shadetotem
  tip Take your weapon from Boarton: the Hoof-Holstered Blade or the Valley Cosh.
  turnin 76240 choose 277988 278002           -- Boarton Shadetotem
